X301 OpenSSL policy overlay
===========================

The base `x301-openssl-provider` package activates the provider but does not
change the system TLS group preference. This optional subpackage installs an
inactive OpenSSL overlay template at:

    /usr/share/x301-openssl-provider/opensslcnf-x301.config

Fedora `.pmod` files reject unregistered provider group names, so this is not a
normal Fedora subpolicy. To enable the overlay explicitly for a laboratory
system using a permissive policy:

    sudo install -Dpm 0644 \
        /usr/share/x301-openssl-provider/opensslcnf-x301.config \
        /etc/crypto-policies/local.d/opensslcnf-zz-x301.config
    sudo update-crypto-policies

Do not enable this overlay under FIPS, BSI, EMPTY, GOST-only or another policy
whose algorithm set must remain closed. Remove it before selecting such a
policy:

    sudo rm -f /etc/crypto-policies/local.d/opensslcnf-zz-x301.config
    sudo update-crypto-policies

Restart long-running OpenSSL applications after either command sequence.
